{"message":"I made a mistake: I enabled roaming on line L1001 (555-123-2001), changing it from disabled to enabled. That is not the phone number you provided, 555-123-2002. I’m sorry for changing the wrong line.

I can correct this by disabling roaming on L1001, returning it to its previous setting. Would you like me to do that?

Your account was found using 555-123-2002, but the data usage and roaming checks above were for the wrong line. Your MMS issue still needs to be investigated on the correct line."}

{"message":"Roaming is now enabled on 555-123-2002; I verified the updated line record. There is no charge for enabling roaming.

Extra data costs $2 per GB, so 2 GB will cost $4, added to your bill. Your mobile plan will remain unchanged, and I haven’t added any data yet.

Do you confirm purchasing 2 GB for $4?"}

{"message":"Please turn Data Roaming ON using toggle_roaming(). Roaming is already enabled on your account for this line.

Then use set_network_mode_preference(mode="4g_5g_preferred") to move away from 2G, which is unsuitable for MMS.

Check your network status again, try browsing a website using mobile data, and retry sending a picture message. Let me know the network type and whether those tests work."}

{"message":"I’ve enabled roaming at no cost on your line ending in 2002. I also corrected an earlier mistake that enabled roaming on your other line, restoring that line’s original setting.

On your phone, turn Data Roaming and Mobile Data on, then restart the device. Check whether signal returns.

If there’s still no signal, please check your SIM status and tell me whether it shows Active, Missing, or Locked. If it shows Missing, remove and reinsert the SIM. If it shows Locked, let me know so I can escalate for SIM security assistance."}

{"message":"Now that your signal is restored, please check whether you can browse a website using mobile data with Wi-Fi off.

If browsing works, check your APN settings using check_apn_settings, especially whether the MMSC URL is missing or marked incorrect. If it is, reset the APN settings to default and restart your phone before testing MMS again.

Does mobile browsing work, and what do the APN/MMSC settings show?"}

{"message":"I won’t make any further changes to the other line. Your number, 555-123-2002, is active, but it has used 15.1 GB against its 15 GB data limit. Exceeding that limit stops mobile data, which MMS needs.

You’ve already tried restarting, resetting the APN, disabling Wi-Fi Calling, and granting messaging permissions. Also, the manual APN details I previously gave you weren’t verified; I’m sorry for that.

For the data limit, you can add up to 2 GB for a charge or explore a plan with more data. Would you like to check the price of adding data? I won’t add anything without your confirmation."}
